<qti-assessment-item xmlns="http://www.imsglobal.org/xsd/imsqtiasi_v3p0" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.imsglobal.org/xsd/imsqtiasi_v3p0 https://purl.imsglobal.org/spec/qti/v3p0/schema/xsd/imsqti_asiv3p0_v1p0.xsd" identifier="pcb-item-61209a9937234b33b1cc09f9e48593ae" title="sat-c2-u24-overstated.html qc1" adaptive="true" time-dependent="false">
  <qti-response-declaration identifier="RESPONSE" cardinality="single" base-type="identifier">
    <qti-correct-response><qti-value>B</qti-value></qti-correct-response>
  </qti-response-declaration>
  <qti-outcome-declaration identifier="SCORE" cardinality="single" base-type="float"><qti-default-value><qti-value>0</qti-value></qti-default-value></qti-outcome-declaration>
  <qti-outcome-declaration identifier="FEEDBACK" cardinality="single" base-type="identifier"/>
  <qti-outcome-declaration identifier="INTERACTION_VISIBILITY" cardinality="single" base-type="identifier">
    <qti-default-value><qti-value>show_interaction</qti-value></qti-default-value>
  </qti-outcome-declaration>
  <qti-item-body>
    <qti-feedback-block identifier="show_interaction" outcome-identifier="INTERACTION_VISIBILITY" show-hide="show" class="qti-margin-0">
      <qti-content-body>
        <p>Which sentence uses &quot;overstated&quot; correctly?</p>
    <qti-choice-interaction response-identifier="RESPONSE" shuffle="true" max-choices="1">
      <qti-simple-choice identifier="A">Critics adored the memoir&apos;s overstated style: bare sentences, flat delivery, feelings barely hinted at anywhere across its three hundred pages.</qti-simple-choice><qti-simple-choice identifier="B">The campaign&apos;s crowd count proved overstated: the plaza holds eight thousand people, and the press office had claimed twenty thousand.</qti-simple-choice><qti-simple-choice identifier="C">The stadium announcer chose an overstated volume setting so that even fans in the very top row could hear every syllable.</qti-simple-choice><qti-simple-choice identifier="D">The movers charged extra because the piano proved overstated for the narrow stairwell and had to come up slowly through the window.</qti-simple-choice>
    </qti-choice-interaction>
      </qti-content-body>
    </qti-feedback-block>

    <qti-feedback-block identifier="FB-A" outcome-identifier="FEEDBACK" show-hide="show">
      <qti-content-body><p>Not quite! Overstated means put more strongly than the facts support, so it&apos;s not the correct choice here because bare sentences and feelings barely hinted at describe restraint — a style that holds back is the reverse of one that pitches claims too high.</p></qti-content-body>
    </qti-feedback-block>
    <qti-feedback-block identifier="FB-B" outcome-identifier="FEEDBACK" show-hide="show">
      <qti-content-body><p>Correct! Overstated means put more strongly than the facts support, so it&apos;s the correct answer because the plaza&apos;s real capacity is eight thousand and the claim was twenty thousand — a genuine crowd, described at more than twice its possible size.</p></qti-content-body>
    </qti-feedback-block>
    <qti-feedback-block identifier="FB-C" outcome-identifier="FEEDBACK" show-hide="show">
      <qti-content-body><p>Not quite! Overstated means put more strongly than the facts support, so it&apos;s not the correct choice here because a volume setting is loudness, not a claim — turning a microphone up cannot pitch any fact past its evidence.</p></qti-content-body>
    </qti-feedback-block>
    <qti-feedback-block identifier="FB-D" outcome-identifier="FEEDBACK" show-hide="show">
      <qti-content-body><p>Not quite! Overstated means put more strongly than the facts support, so it&apos;s not the correct choice here because a piano that cannot fit a stairwell is oversized — a matter of physical bulk, not of claims made about it.</p></qti-content-body>
    </qti-feedback-block>
  </qti-item-body>
  <qti-response-processing>
    <qti-response-condition>
    <qti-response-if>
      <qti-match><qti-variable identifier="RESPONSE"/><qti-base-value base-type="identifier">A</qti-base-value></qti-match>
      <qti-set-outcome-value identifier="SCORE"><qti-base-value base-type="float">0</qti-base-value></qti-set-outcome-value>
      <qti-set-outcome-value identifier="FEEDBACK"><qti-base-value base-type="identifier">FB-A</qti-base-value></qti-set-outcome-value>
    
        <qti-set-outcome-value identifier="completionStatus"><qti-base-value base-type="identifier">incomplete</qti-base-value></qti-set-outcome-value></qti-response-if>
    </qti-response-condition>
    <qti-response-condition>
    <qti-response-if>
      <qti-match><qti-variable identifier="RESPONSE"/><qti-base-value base-type="identifier">B</qti-base-value></qti-match>
      <qti-set-outcome-value identifier="SCORE"><qti-base-value base-type="float">1</qti-base-value></qti-set-outcome-value>
      <qti-set-outcome-value identifier="FEEDBACK"><qti-base-value base-type="identifier">FB-B</qti-base-value></qti-set-outcome-value>
    
        <qti-set-outcome-value identifier="completionStatus"><qti-base-value base-type="identifier">completed</qti-base-value></qti-set-outcome-value></qti-response-if>
    </qti-response-condition>
    <qti-response-condition>
    <qti-response-if>
      <qti-match><qti-variable identifier="RESPONSE"/><qti-base-value base-type="identifier">C</qti-base-value></qti-match>
